General Rules
System Stability:

Ensure that the application is stable and performs efficiently under various loads.
All data must be stored securely to prevent data breaches.
User Authentication:

Customers and administrators must authenticate before accessing sensitive information.
Use secure password protocols and multi-factor authentication for admin access.
Data Privacy:

Collect only necessary customer information.
Encrypt all sensitive data such as billing details and customer profiles.
Billing and Real-Time Processing
Item Scanning:

Support both barcode and QR code scanning for item identification.
Ensure instant response time for scanning and adding items to the bill.
Billing Calculations:

Automatically calculate item prices, taxes, and discounts in real-time.
Ensure accuracy in the subtotal, tax, and total amounts displayed.
Customer Information:

Link billed items to the corresponding customer profile.
Allow quick retrieval and update of customer data during billing.
Analytics Dashboard
Real-Time Insights:

Display real-time sales data, including daily, weekly, and monthly summaries.
Include visual representations such as graphs and charts for better understanding.
Performance Metrics:

Show key performance indicators like top-selling products, revenue trends, and customer demographics.
Custom Reports:

Enable generation of custom reports based on selected timeframes or specific metrics.
Environmental Impact Tab
Sustainability Metrics:

Show statistics on paperless billing, energy usage, and carbon footprint reduction.
Provide actionable tips for improving the environmental impact of the system.
Recyclable Packaging:

Highlight products using recyclable or eco-friendly packaging.
Scan Page
Barcode/QR Code Scanning:

Ensure smooth and error-free scanning using the device camera or an external scanner.
Handle both 1D and 2D barcodes effectively.
Fallback Mechanism:

Allow manual entry of product codes in case of scanning failure.
Scan Accuracy:

Validate scanned data to ensure the correct product is added to the bill.
Error Handling and Notifications
Error Messages:

Display user-friendly error messages for system issues like failed scans or database errors.
Notifications:

Notify users of successful transactions, low inventory levels, or other important system events.
Security and Maintenance
Regular Updates:

Perform regular updates to keep the system secure and up-to-date with the latest features.
Data Backup:

Automatically back up data to prevent loss in case of system failure.
Access Control:

Implement role-based access to different sections of the system (e.g., admin, cashier, customer).
